course: dictionary
lesson: 14733
title: Words that say no
level: primary-4
stars: 0
explain: Prohibited means not allowed. A law or a rule says you must not do something. «Smoking is prohibited in this park.» The sign tells you what you must not do there.
explain: Context gives you clues. «No bikes allowed» and «Bikes prohibited» mean the same thing. Swap in not allowed and check: «Bikes not allowed» still makes sense, so prohibited must mean not allowed.
explain: Prohibited is also the past form of the verb prohibit. «The rules prohibited running in the corridor» tells you that a rule stopped people from running. Prohibit, prohibits, prohibited and prohibiting all come from the same word.
fact: Prohibited means not allowed by a law or a rule; forbidden.
fact: «Strictly prohibited» means very firmly not allowed.
fact: «Prohibited items» are things you must not take into a place, such as on a plane.
fact: Prohibit is the verb. Its forms are prohibits, prohibited and prohibiting.
fact: «Prohibited from» means stopped from doing something by a rule or by force, as in «She was prohibited from entering the room.»
exercise: «Smoking is prohibited in this park.» What does prohibited mean? | Only for children | *Not allowed | Very dirty | Free to use
exercise: A sign says «Entry prohibited». What should you do? | *Do not go in | Walk in quickly | Run to the door | Ask for a sticker
exercise: Find the past form of prohibit in «The rules prohibited running in the corridor.» | prohibits | prohibiting | *prohibited | prohibit
test: «Liquids over 100 ml are prohibited in your hand luggage.» What does this tell you? | Your bag is very heavy | You must always carry liquids in your hand luggage | Liquids are cheap to buy | *You must not take them in your hand luggage
test: «Ella was prohibited from using the lift.» What does this mean? | Ella loved the lift very much | Ella was told to clean the lift | Ella was given a prize for using the lift | *A rule stopped Ella from using the lift
exam: Which of these would be a prohibited item in hand luggage on a plane? | A pencil case | A book | *A sharp knife | A pair of socks
